### Catalog (run http/auth.http and http/stores.http first: accessToken, storeId)

@base = http://localhost:8080

### Create a product with two variants
POST {{base}}/admin/v1/stores/{{storeId}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Classic Tee", "status": "ACTIVE", "vendor": "Acme", "options": ["Size", "Color"],
 "variants": [
   {"sku": "TEE-M-RED", "price": "19.99", "compareAtPrice": "24.99", "options": ["M", "Red"]},
   {"sku": "TEE-L-RED", "price": "21.50", "options": ["L", "Red"]}]}

> {% client.global.set("productId", response.body.id); client.global.set("etag", response.headers.valueOf("ETag")); %}

### Edit with optimistic concurrency (repeat with the old ETag to see 412)
PATCH {{base}}/admin/v1/stores/{{storeId}}/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
If-Match: {{etag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Classic Tee 2.0"}

### List (filters: status, vendor, q; sort: -createdAt | createdAt)
GET {{base}}/admin/v1/stores/{{storeId}}/products?status=ACTIVE&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Public storefront (store chosen by hostname; replace "acme" with your store handle)
GET {{base}}/storefront/v1/products
X-Forwarded-Host: acme.storeforge.localhost

### Single product by handle
GET {{base}}/storefront/v1/products/classic-tee
X-Forwarded-Host: acme.storeforge.localhost
